3]],[2026,[0,0,0,0,0]]]},"story":{"fwci":["Typical work: for works published 2015–2022, the median FWCI is 0–0.15. In every year, half of the works received at most 15% of the citations expected for similar works worldwide (FWCI 1 = world average).","Above the world average: 2%–8% of the works per year have an FWCI above 1, most in 2021 (8%).","Not cited: on average 59% of these works have FWCI 0, meaning no citations within their four-year window. That is why many boxes start at 0.","Mean versus median: the mean is above the median in 4 of 4 years, because a few highly cited works pull the average up. The widest gap is 2021: mean 0.37, median 0.15, top work 5.95. The median is the better guide to a typical work.","Still counting: works from 2023–2025 have not completed their four-year citation window, so their values will rise. Do not compare them with older years yet.","Small base: the values for 2011–2012, 2016–2018, 2020 and 2025 are based on only 10–29 works (lighter box or hollow point), so read them with care.","Few works: 2004, 2013–2014 and 2026 have fewer than 10 works, too few for a box. Each of those works is drawn as a dot."],"citations":["Typical work: works published 2015–2023 have a median of 0–2 citations each; the highest median (2) is in 2019.","Most cited works: the top 10% of works published in 2019 have at least 10 citations each, the highest P90 in the chart.","Not yet cited: more than half of the works published 2023–2025 have no citations so far. This is expected for recent works and is not a sign of low quality.","Mean versus median: the mean is above the median in 5 of 5 years, because a few highly cited works pull the average up. The widest gap is 2021: mean 3.9, median 1.5, top work 88. The median is the better guide to a typical work.","Recent years: works from 2024–2025 have had less than three years to be cited, so their values will rise.","Small base: the values for 2011–2012, 2016–2018, 2020 and 2025 are based on only 10–29 works (lighter box or hollow point), so read them with care.","Few works: 2004, 2013–2014 and 2026 have fewer than 10 works, too few for a band. Each of those works is drawn as a dot."]}}}